Data

- Prices: the task packs under data/ are derived from ERCOT's Day-Ahead Market settlement point prices for the
  hubs and load zones (report NP4-180-ER, "Historical DAM Load Zone and Hub Prices"), published by the Electric
  Reliability Council of Texas, Inc. (ERCOT) at https://www.ercot.com/mp/data-products/data-product-details?id=NP4-180-ER.
  They are used under ERCOT's Website User Agreement (https://www.ercot.com/help/terms), section 5, which data/LICENSE
  quotes in full with the Market Data Transparency Terms of Use v1.2. The ERCOT data is not relicensed under
  Apache-2.0 or any Creative Commons licence. Source: ERCOT. ERCOT does not endorse this product or any result derived
  from it, is not affiliated with it, and is not responsible for its accuracy. No ERCOT logo or trademark is used.
- Battery archetypes: sized from the U.S. Energy Information Administration's Form EIA-860 annual electric
  generator data, 2025 (https://www.eia.gov/electricity/data/eia860/), a work of the U.S. Government in the public
  domain. Source: U.S. Energy Information Administration.
- Weather in the viewer: ASOS observations at each point's representative airport, from the Iowa Environmental
  Mesonet (IEM), Iowa State University (https://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu/); NWS and FAA observations in the public
  domain, credited as the IEM asks. Fetched into cache/weather, not distributed in data/.
- v3 preview: the regulation drift is derived from ERCOT's 60-Day SCED Disclosure (NP3-965-ER), reduced to the
  storage fleet's hourly deployment share, obtained through ERCOT's Public API under ERCOT's terms.
- v4 and v5 previews: ERCOT's posted load, wind and solar forecasts (NP3-565-CD, NP4-732-CD, NP4-742-CD, NP4-745-CD),
  the 60-Day DAM Disclosure (NP3-966-ER, aggregated and anonymised) and DAM System Lambda (NP4-523-CD), obtained
  through ERCOT's Public API under ERCOT's terms; NOAA HRRR model runs (NOAA Open Data Dissemination, public domain)
  and EIA-930 hourly data (public domain). Bulletins are paraphrased. See data/LICENSE, sections 4 to 6.
